cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the archived software release and the associated article."
title: "PREFLIGHT-PT: code for compiled-circuit Clifford probes on QAOA workloads"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vishwakarma
    given-names: Aishwarya
    affiliation: "Department of Quantum Matter Physics, University of Geneva"
    email: aishwarya.vishwakarma@unige.ch
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-11-07
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23782910
repository-code: "https://github.com/vishwaka-2419/preflight-pt-qaoa"
abstract: >-
  Code-only release of the Python scripts for constructing, submitting and
  analysing compiled-circuit Clifford probes and QAOA workload experiments on
  IBM Heron processors. Version 1.0.1 adds the corrected output pairing as a
  builder option (the default reproduces the executed circuits), the recovery
  of the readout-pair statistic from the executed measurements, and the
  analysis scripts for the variants of the statistic, the direct-sampling
  comparison, the paired comparisons and the noise-model simulation. Research
  data are not included; the derived per-edge correlator record and analysis
  tables accompany the article as Supplementary Data.
license: MIT
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - QAOA
  - Clifford circuits
  - IBM Quantum
  - quantum benchmarking
  - calibration
